  "workedSolution": "1. Halving every 6 days: $\\mathrm{e}^{-6k} = \\frac{1}{2}$, so $k = \\frac{\\ln 2}{6}$. Then $\\mathrm{e}^{-kt} = \\frac{5}{80} = \\frac{1}{16}$, so $kt = \\ln 16 = 4\\ln 2$ and $t = \\frac{4\\ln 2}{\\ln 2 / 6} = 24$ days. (80 → 40 → 20 → 10 → 5 is four halvings.)",
  "hints": [
   "Use the halving information to find k.",
